# Reference: Gail Grant, "Technical Manual and Dictionary of Classical Ballet" (Elevé: rise from straight legs)
# Reference: Agrippina Vaganova, "Basic Principles of Classical Ballet"
# Review status: Experimental (ballet UAT; pending peer review with dance-domain educator)
# Biomechanical note: Elevé is a smooth rise directly from straight legs onto demi-pointe (balls of feet)
# in first position without an intervening plié. Turnout (~30° hip external rotation) and upright
# vertical spine are sustained throughout the rise and controlled lowering.

posecode exercise "Elevé"
  rig humanoid
  pose start = first-position

  step "Rise" 1.8s settle:
    ankles: plantarflex 30
    knees: extend 0
    shoulders: abduct 70
    elbows: flex 15
    spine: extend 4
    ground-lock: feet
    cue "Rise onto the balls of the feet with heels pressing forward, maintaining turnout and tall spine"

  step "Lower" 2s settle:
    ankles: plantarflex 0
    knees: extend 0
    shoulders: abduct 70
    elbows: flex 15
    spine: extend 4
    ground-lock: feet
    cue "Lower the heels with control, sustaining turnout and vertical spine back to first position"

  repeat 5
